$DIR/main.p:8:2: bit field offset (bits 4 to 16) crosses a byte boundary in a big-endian packed type
    A big-endian packed type with a byte array, a []byte or no backing numbers
    its bits byte by byte, and stores a field of several bytes with its most
    significant byte first. A bit field may not cross a byte boundary, since
    there is no single order for its bits. A field of whole bytes (a uint16,
    say) must start on a byte boundary.
    Put the field in a packed type of its own with an integer backing, and use
    that type as a field. The nested type is then laid out as an integer,
    whatever the bytes around it.
    (see "packed types" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.14)
    (run "pluto explain E2021" for a longer explanation)

